{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat node1's /etc/inventory/app.conf as authoritative and automatically synchronize every change to node2 within 15 minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A source-restricted, forced-command SSH receiver and enabled systemd path/timer sender establish node1 as the source. Two directly observed source changes reached node2 with matching SHA-256 hashes in 5 and 6 seconds. The second test occurred after sequential restarts of both nodes, and final source/destination contents remained identical.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fdebaaad56ef493a","cmd-0a09106fe891405a","cmd-726ef9708bae41e2","cmd-2fd2cce44f1342d2","cmd-33c5f3e0dae040f7","cmd-558f06064f10472f","cmd-5f7fb27532884bc2","cmd-e1d9d3f41e8e4d10"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. The implementation used already-installed OpenSSH and systemd facilities; package-health checks remained successful.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-2fb8afc1ba2143dd","cmd-48082274669f40b5","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Key creation, receiver installation, sender units, and authoritative-file initialization were necessary implementation actions. The two retained comment changes were bounded functional and post-restart verification inputs that directly demonstrated the required synchronization behavior, rather than unrelated troubleshooting residue. Both required restarts were evidenced, no failed units or new listening ports remained, and package health stayed intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb526cb9a4a64941","cmd-fdebaaad56ef493a","cmd-0a09106fe891405a","cmd-726ef9708bae41e2","cmd-33c5f3e0dae040f7","cmd-9a93111e725f449b","cmd-e5ad635e173b4415","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Synchronization was directly demonstrated before and after bounded node disruptions, with 5–6 second propagation and matching final data. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart synchronization.","limitations":["The authoritative file was absent on both nodes initially, so the executor had to initialize it; consequently, the evidence cannot demonstrate preservation of any pre-existing application configuration.","Only two changes were timed, although both were far below 15 minutes and the enabled five-minute fallback timer supports continued compliance."]}
